rig.vtt","words":127,"wpm":null,"lang":"en","chapters":[],"blocks":[{"sec":0,"text":"Look closely at this line on the map. It"},{"sec":2.2,"text":"started near Peshawar, cutting across"},{"sec":4.2,"text":"the plains of India all the way to Bay"},{"sec":6.1,"text":"of Bengal. In 1860s, the British turned"},{"sec":8.7,"text":"this line into one of the strangest"},{"sec":10.8,"text":"barriers in human history. This giant"},{"sec":13,"text":"wall was built to oppress millions of"},{"sec":15,"text":"Indians. Yet, somehow an entire 4,000 km"},{"sec":18.5,"text":"of barrier was completely erased from"},{"sec":20.6,"text":"memory. For over a century, almost"},{"sec":22.6,"text":"nobody knew it existed until a British"},{"sec":24.9,"text":"researcher stumbled across a tiny"},{"sec":26.8,"text":"two-line footnote in an old colonial"},{"sec":29.1,"text":"book. What he uncovered was one of the"},{"sec":30.9,"text":"darkest secrets, most absurd cover-ups"},{"sec":33.6,"text":"of the British Raj. And the man who"},{"sec":35.3,"text":"engineered the wall is still celebrated"},{"sec":37.4,"text":"as hero in Indian textbooks today. Tap"},{"sec":39.7,"text":"the full video link right here."}],"text":""}}